In the clip, the singer appears in a recording studio, reading the lyrics from her phone as she records and sings into the mic. Shots from different angles of her body appear before she’s seen walking toward the mic, then turning around to reveal her baby bump. Meanwhile, her new song “Haven” plays in the background. “As one chapter ends, another begins,” the artist captioned the post, adding a heart and a pregnant woman emoji.

Pinnock and Gray, who were married in a beachfront ceremony in Jamaica in 2023, have two other children, twin daughters born in 2021.

Fellow members of Little Mix expressed their happiness on the post with Perrie Edwards commenting with heart-eyes emojis and Jade Thirlwall sharing a message celebrating the news of Pinnock’s growing family.&nbsp;

The news arrives at a major moment for Pinnock’s music career. She released her debut solo album My Ego Told Me To in February, and she announced a U.K. and European tour to promote the project.&nbsp;&nbsp;

Little Mix, which was formed in 2011 on The X Factor in the U.K., earned various Billboard chart entries, including three of the girl group’s albums, DNA, Salute and Glory Days, reaching the Billboard 200 . In 2021, their single “Confetti” became their final song before they announced a hiatus.
